From cf95bc9c97327409d6fc834b7299f5594a63faac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:59:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BACKPORT: f2fs: introduce gc_merge mount option

Backport the F2FS GC merge mount option from the Samsung Exynos 2400
Linux 6.1 tree (android14-6.1-S921BXXSDCZB2), based on upstream commit
5911d2d1d1a38b26585383478bd71d9254e48bdf.

When enabled, the background GC thread handles foreground GC requests
and merges them with ongoing background GC. This avoids slow foreground
GC in a process context when free space is low and can reduce UI stalls
during storage-heavy operations.

Local compatibility changes for the Exynos9820 4.14 F2FS:
- adapt to the target's 4-argument f2fs_gc() API;
- use the target's f2fs_down_write()/f2fs_up_write() wrappers;
- keep the target's GC urgent/sleep handling;
- start the GC thread when gc_merge is set even if background_gc=off;
- add the mount option and documentation to the target tree.

Audit corrections:
- wake foreground GC waiters on read-only, frozen-filesystem, and
  sb_start_write_trylock() skip paths;
- keep the published gc_thread allocation alive until superblock
  teardown, use f2fs_gc_task as the running marker, and recheck it after
  prepare_to_wait() to avoid finish_wait() on freed waitqueue storage;
- submit cached OPU/IPU DATA bios before merged or direct foreground GC
  to avoid the gc_merge DATA-bio deadlock;
- do not run background GC when background_gc=off unless the request is
  foreground or urgent.

Final pre-application correction:
- serialize GC-thread stop in the shutdown ioctl against remount and
  other shutdown callers through sb->s_umount.

Upstream commit: 5911d2d1d1a38b26585383478bd71d9254e48bdf
Original-author: Chao Yu <yuchao0@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: @Devandroid-bit.
